## Exp49 — Symmetric Boundary-Proximity Timing Family — FROZEN BEFORE SCORE

Purpose: test a mechanistically defined timing family for EXIT-vs-NO_EXIT. This is not indicator search. The causal universe is distance/proximity to the two fixed active corridor boundaries at state_time.

Exact universe remains unchanged: same historical cutoff, exact dynamic states, exact Exp41 eligible 15/30/60/120m cells, exact 8 Exp44/45 direction×time environments, whole-BRT-day inference, no Exp27 access.

At each state_time compute with the already-frozen corridor and current ATR:

d_back_atr = bias_sign*(close-back)/ATR > 0
d_forward_atr = bias_sign*(forward-close)/ATR > 0
Position = d_back_atr/(d_back_atr+d_forward_atr)

Frozen timing candidates, all fixed before scoring:
T1 EDGE_REL = abs(2*Position-1). 0=center, 1=near an edge in relative geometry.
T2 LOG_NEAR_ATR = log1p(min(d_back_atr,d_forward_atr)).
T3 LOG_FAR_ATR = log1p(max(d_back_atr,d_forward_atr)).
T4 LOG_HARMONIC_ATR = log1p(2*d_back_atr*d_forward_atr/(d_back_atr+d_forward_atr)).

Rationale: binary EXIT timing should be symmetric to which side wins. T1 measures relative edge proximity; T2 absolute distance to the nearest escape boundary; T3 far-boundary context; T4 two-sided escape depth. No sign of Position is used as a timing predictor.

Model family: discrete-time binary EXIT hazard on the original person-period table. y_exit_step=1 when current step exits by either ADVANCE or RECAPTURE, else 0 while at risk. All models fit TRAIN only with the same 24 elapsed-step intercepts.

BASE_EXIT = 24 step intercepts only.
EDGE_EXIT = BASE_EXIT + T1.
NEAR_EXIT = BASE_EXIT + T2.
FAR_EXIT = BASE_EXIT + T3.
HARM_EXIT = BASE_EXIT + T4.
JOINT4_EXIT = BASE_EXIT + T1+T2+T3+T4.

No hyperparameter tuning, no threshold, no alternate transforms after result. Standardization, if needed numerically, must use TRAIN mean/std only and be fixed for VAL/TEST.

Required analysis is one frozen family analysis: marginal candidate diagnostics; TRAIN-only feature correlation/redundancy report; JOINT4; drop-one from JOINT4; horizon 15/30/60/120 cumulative EXIT probabilities; calibration and EXIT AUC diagnostics; whole-BRT-day bootstrap; multiplicity-aware marginal reporting. TEST may not rescue a failed family result.

Primary family comparison: JOINT4_EXIT vs BASE_EXIT using binary Brier and LogLoss on EXIT_STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED cells within each of the exact 8 environments. Environment must contain EXIT and NO_EXIT and >=2 BRT days. Formal FAMILY PASS requires CI95 lower bound >0 for both metrics in all 8 environments = 16/16.

TIMING_GEOMETRY_FAMILY=PASS only at 16/16 for JOINT4 vs BASE.
ROBUST_SYMMETRIC_EXIT_GEOMETRY=PASS only if all environments scorable, JOINT4 16/16, and the joint fit is numerically identifiable. Marginal or drop-one diagnostics cannot rescue a JOINT4 formal failure.

Anti-rescue: no Dwell; no signed Position timing rescue; no alternate EXIT definition; no side conditioning; no horizon subset; no dropped environment; no side/era-specific fit; no direction×time interaction; no recalibration/intercept/threshold rescue; no alternate transforms; no additional feature after result; no Validation/TEST refit; no Exp27 scoring/modification.

Exp49 failure cannot erase Exp44/45/47 PASS results. Historical OOS remains exploratory; runtime promotion NONE.
